 # @acme/ui
 
-Accessible React components.
+Accessible React 19 components: `Tabs`, `Dialog`, and `Combobox`. No CSS is shipped; every component accepts `className` and forwards other native props to the element it renders.
+
+User event handlers passed as props (`onKeyDown`, `onBlur`, `onMouseDown`, and so on) run first, before the component's own logic. For key handlers, calling `event.preventDefault()` skips the built-in key handling for that event.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm test       # vitest run
+pnpm typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
+```
+
+Import from the package entry, `src/index.ts`:
+
+```ts
+import { Tabs, TabList, Tab, TabPanel, Dialog, Combobox } from "./src";
+```
+
+Ids come from `React.useId`, so several instances can share a page.
+
+## Tabs
+
+`Tabs` owns the selection. `TabList` renders the `tablist`, `Tab` the buttons, and `TabPanel` the panels. Non-selected panels get `hidden`.
+
+### Tabs props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` | optional | Selected tab. Passing it makes the component controlled. |
+| `defaultValue` | `string` | optional, first enabled tab | Initial selection when uncontrolled. A missing or disabled value falls back to the first enabled tab. |
+| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` | optional | Called when the user selects a different tab. Not called for re-selecting the current tab or for the automatic fallback. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the wrapper `div`. Other `div` props are forwarded. |
+
+### TabList props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `aria-label` | `string` | required | Accessible name of the tablist. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the `role="tablist"` element. Other `div` props are forwarded. |
+
+### Tab props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` | required | Identifies the tab. The matching `TabPanel` uses the same value. |
+| `disabled` | `boolean` | optional, `false` | Skipped by the keyboard; clicks are ignored. Rendered with `aria-disabled="true"`, so it stays discoverable. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the button. Other button props are forwarded, except `type`. |
+
+### TabPanel props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `value` | `string` | required | The tab this panel belongs to. Hidden unless it is selected. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the `role="tabpanel"` element. Other `div` props are forwarded. |
+
+### Tabs keyboard
+
+| Key | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Tab` | Moves into the tablist on the selected tab, then to the selected panel. |
+| `ArrowRight` / `ArrowLeft` | Focus and select the next / previous enabled tab. Wraps at the ends and skips disabled tabs. |
+| `Home` / `End` | Focus and select the first / last enabled tab. |
+
+Tab order follows the DOM order of the tabs, including tabs inserted after mount. Only the selected tab has `tabIndex=0`. If the selected tab is missing or disabled, the first enabled tab gets `tabIndex=0` instead, so the tablist stays reachable by keyboard. Uncontrolled, that tab is also selected. Controlled, `aria-selected` follows `value` even when it names a disabled tab (for example `value="three"` with `three` disabled); the tab stop still moves to the first enabled tab. A missing value (for example `value="nope"`) leaves no tab marked selected.
+
+### Tabs example
+
+```tsx
+// Uncontrolled
+<Tabs defaultValue="profile">
+  <TabList aria-label="Settings">
+    <Tab value="profile">Profile</Tab>
+    <Tab value="billing">Billing</Tab>
+  </TabList>
+  <TabPanel value="profile">Profile form</TabPanel>
+  <TabPanel value="billing">Billing form</TabPanel>
+</Tabs>
+
+// Controlled
+const [tab, setTab] = useState("profile");
+<Tabs value={tab} onValueChange={setTab}>
+  {/* same TabList and TabPanels */}
+</Tabs>
+```
+
+## Dialog
+
+A modal dialog rendered into `document.body`, with a backdrop. It is controlled only: the parent owns `open`.
+
+### Dialog props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `open` | `boolean` | required | Whether the dialog is shown. Renders nothing when `false`. |
+| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` | required | Called with `false` on Escape or a backdrop click. The component never closes itself; the parent must set `open`. |
+| `title` | `string` | required | Rendered as an `h2` and used as the accessible name. |
+| `description` | `string` | optional | Rendered below the title and linked with `aria-describedby`. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the `role="dialog"` element. Other `div` props are forwarded. |
+
+Behavior:
+
+- On open, focus moves to the first tabbable element. An element with `autoFocus` keeps focus. With no tabbable element, the dialog itself is focused.
+- Focus is trapped. Tab and Shift+Tab cycle through the tabbable elements, computed at keypress time. Disabled, `hidden`, `tabIndex=-1`, `type="hidden"` inputs, and `inert` content is skipped. Focus that leaves the dialog is brought back.
+- On close (or unmount while open), focus returns to the element focused before opening, if it is still in the document.
+- A click counts as a backdrop click only when both the press and the release happen on the backdrop.
+- Nested dialogs stack. Only the topmost handles Escape and Tab.
+
+### Dialog keyboard
+
+| Key | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` | Move through the dialog's tabbable elements, wrapping at both ends. |
+| `Escape` | Calls `onOpenChange(false)` for the topmost dialog only. |
+
+### Dialog example
+
+```tsx
+// Controlled (the only mode)
+const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
+<button onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>Delete account</button>
+<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} title="Delete account" description="This cannot be undone.">
+  <button onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>Cancel</button>
+  <button>Delete</button>
+</Dialog>
+```
+
+## Combobox
+
+A text input that filters a list of options. The component is controlled: `value` and `onChange` are required.
+
+### Combobox props
+
+| Name | Type | Required / default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `label` | `string` | required | Visible label, associated with the input. |
+| `options` | `ComboboxOption<T>[]` | required | `{ value: T; label: string; disabled?: boolean }`. `T extends string`, default `string`. |
+| `value` | `T \| null` | required | Selected option value, or `null` for none. A value matching no option shows an empty input. |
+| `onChange` | `(value: T \| null) => void` | required | Called when the user commits an option, or clears the selection (see below). |
+| `placeholder` | `string` | optional | Forwarded to the input. |
+| `className` | `string` | optional | Applied to the `role="combobox"` input. Other input props are forwarded, except `value`, `defaultValue`, `onChange`, `role`, and `type`. |
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Typing opens the popup and filters options by case-insensitive substring of `label`. The query is literal; regex characters match only themselves. An empty query shows every option.
+- The active option is tracked by value and exposed through `aria-activedescendant`. DOM focus stays on the input. Disabled options are skipped and never selected.
+- If the active option is filtered out or removed, it becomes inactive. Nothing is active until an arrow key is pressed.
+- Clicking an enabled option commits it. Clicking a disabled option does nothing. Option mousedown is prevented, so the input keeps focus.
+- Clearing the text and then blurring, or pressing Enter with no active option, calls `onChange(null)` once. Nothing is called if the value is already `null`.
+- Blur closes the popup and reverts the text to the selected label, without `onChange` unless the text was cleared.
+- The component never changes the displayed selection on its own. The displayed text follows the `value` prop.
+- With the popup open, Escape stops propagation so an enclosing dialog stays open.
+
+### Combobox keyboard
+
+| Key | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `ArrowDown` / `ArrowUp` | Open the popup if closed, then move the active option to the next / previous enabled option. Wraps. |
+| `Alt+ArrowDown` / `Alt+ArrowUp` | Open the popup without moving the active option. |
+| `Enter` | Commit the active option. With no active option and cleared text, clear the selection (`onChange(null)`). Otherwise does nothing. |
+| `Escape` | Close the popup, revert the text to the selected label, no `onChange`. When already closed, only reverts the text. |
+| `Tab` (blur) | Closes the popup; see blur behavior above. |
+
+A user `onKeyDown` runs before these rows. If it calls `preventDefault()`, none of them run for that key.
+
+### Combobox example
+
+```tsx
+// Controlled
+const [fruit, setFruit] = useState<string | null>(null);
+<Combobox
+  label="Fruit"
+  options={[
+    { value: "apple", label: "Apple" },
+    { value: "banana", label: "Banana", disabled: true },
+  ]}
+  value={fruit}
+  onChange={setFruit}
+/>
+
+// Uncontrolled use is not supported: pass `value` and `onChange` even if the value never changes.
+```
